const CHRISTMAS_VERSES = "# Christmas Lantern — Scripture Gifts (CSB)\n\nCSB wording supplied by Daniel from Blue Letter Bible on November 11, 2026. Headlines and context notes are editorial, not Scripture quotations. Each card keeps a short focus passage with a folded Read in context section. Supplied selections are preserved with verse numbers; gaps are identified rather than filled with invented text.\n\nScripture quotations marked CSB have been taken from the Christian Standard Bible®, Copyright © 2017, 2020 by Holman Bible Publishers. Used by permission. Christian Standard Bible® and CSB® are federally registered trademarks of Holman Bible Publishers.\n\n## Isaiah 9:2 (CSB)\n\n### A great light\n\nThe people walking in darkness have seen a great light; a light has dawned on those living in the land of darkness.\n\n*Tags: light, promise*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-01\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Isaiah 9:1-7\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Isaiah moves from darkness and oppression to light, deliverance, and a promised royal child. Read the child's rule and peace within that whole promise, rather than treating the names as an isolated holiday slogan.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Isaiah 9:2, 6 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 2,\n      \"text\": \"The people walking in darkness have seen a great light; a light has dawned on those living in the land of darkness.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 6,\n      \"text\": \"For a child will be born for us, a son will be given to us, and the government will be on his shoulders. He will be named Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Eternal Father, Prince of Peace.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"isa\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 9\n}\n```\n\n## Isaiah 9:6 (CSB)\n\n### Unto us a child is born\n\nFor a child will be born for us, a son will be given to us, and the government will be on his shoulders. He will be named Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Eternal Father, Prince of Peace.\n\n*Tags: promise, nativity*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-02\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Isaiah 9:1-7\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Isaiah moves from darkness and oppression to light, deliverance, and a promised royal child. Read the child's rule and peace within that whole promise, rather than treating the names as an isolated holiday slogan.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Isaiah 9:2, 6 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 2,\n      \"text\": \"The people walking in darkness have seen a great light; a light has dawned on those living in the land of darkness.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 6,\n      \"text\": \"For a child will be born for us, a son will be given to us, and the government will be on his shoulders. He will be named Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Eternal Father, Prince of Peace.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"isa\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 9\n}\n```\n\n## Micah 5:2 (CSB)\n\n### Little Bethlehem\n\nBethlehem Ephrathah, you are small among the clans of Judah; one will come from you to be ruler over Israel for me. His origin is from antiquity, from ancient times.\n\n*Tags: bethlehem, promise*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-03\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Micah 5:1-6\",\n  \"context_note\": \"The promise of a ruler from small Bethlehem stands amid siege and threatened invasion. The surrounding verses describe his shepherding and the security he brings to his people.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Micah 5:2-4 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 2,\n      \"text\": \"Bethlehem Ephrathah, you are small among the clans of Judah; one will come from you to be ruler over Israel for me. His origin is from antiquity, from ancient times.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 3,\n      \"text\": \"Therefore, Israel will be abandoned until the time when she who is in labor has given birth; then the rest of the ruler's brothers will return to the people of Israel.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 4,\n      \"text\": \"He will stand and shepherd them in the strength of the LORD, in the majestic name of the LORD his God. They will live securely, for then his greatness will extend to the ends of the earth.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"mic\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 5\n}\n```\n\n## Matthew 1:21 (CSB)\n\n### You shall call his name Jesus\n\n\"She will give birth to a son, and you are to name him Jesus, because he will save his people from their sins.\"\n\n*Tags: nativity, birth*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-04\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Matthew 1:18-25\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Matthew tells how Joseph learns about Mary's child and obeys the angel. The names Jesus and Immanuel belong to this account of his birth, his saving mission, and God's presence.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Matthew 1:21, 23 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 21,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"She will give birth to a son, and you are to name him Jesus, because he will save his people from their sins.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 23,\n      \"text\": \"See, the virgin will become pregnant and give birth to a son, and they will name him Immanuel, which is translated \\\"God is with us.\\\"\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"mat\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 1\n}\n```\n\n## Matthew 1:23 (CSB)\n\n### God with us\n\nSee, the virgin will become pregnant and give birth to a son, and they will name him Immanuel, which is translated \"God is with us.\"\n\n*Tags: nativity, birth*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-05\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Matthew 1:18-25\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Matthew tells how Joseph learns about Mary's child and obeys the angel. The names Jesus and Immanuel belong to this account of his birth, his saving mission, and God's presence.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Matthew 1:21, 23 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 21,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"She will give birth to a son, and you are to name him Jesus, because he will save his people from their sins.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 23,\n      \"text\": \"See, the virgin will become pregnant and give birth to a son, and they will name him Immanuel, which is translated \\\"God is with us.\\\"\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"mat\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 1\n}\n```\n\n## Luke 1:30-31 (CSB)\n\n### Do not be afraid, Mary\n\nThen the angel told her, \"Do not be afraid, Mary, for you have found favor with God. \"Now listen: You will conceive and give birth to a son, and you will name him Jesus.\n\n*Tags: nativity, birth*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-06\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Luke 1:26-38\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Gabriel's announcement includes Jesus' kingship and Mary's question about the birth. Her answer is a response to God's promise and initiative, not a claim that she can accomplish it herself.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Luke 1:30-38 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 30,\n      \"text\": \"Then the angel told her, \\\"Do not be afraid, Mary, for you have found favor with God.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 31,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"Now listen: You will conceive and give birth to a son, and you will name him Jesus.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 32,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"He will be great and will be called the Son of the Most High, and the Lord God will give him the throne of his father David.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 33,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"He will reign over the house of Jacob forever, and his kingdom will have no end.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 34,\n      \"text\": \"Mary asked the angel, \\\"How can this be, since I have not had sexual relations with a man? \\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 35,\n      \"text\": \"The angel replied to her, \\\"The Holy Spirit will come upon you, and the power of the Most High will overshadow you. Therefore, the holy one to be born will be called the Son of God.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 36,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"And consider your relative Elizabeth -- even she has conceived a son in her old age, and this is the sixth month for her who was called childless.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 37,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"For nothing will be impossible with God.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 38,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"See, I am the Lord's servant,\\\" said Mary. \\\"May it happen to me as you have said.\\\" Then the angel left her.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"luk\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 1\n}\n```\n\n## Luke 2:6-7 (CSB)\n\n### A baby in a manger\n\nWhile they were there, the time came for her to give birth. Then she gave birth to her firstborn son, and she wrapped him tightly in cloth and laid him in a manger, because there was no guest room available for them.\n\n*Tags: nativity, birth*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-07\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Luke 2:1-20\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Read the birth, the angel's message, the shepherds' visit, and Mary's pondering as one narrative. The announcement identifies the child as Savior, Messiah, and Lord; the shepherds then go to see him.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Luke 2:6-7, 10-14, 19 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 6,\n      \"text\": \"While they were there, the time came for her to give birth.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 7,\n      \"text\": \"Then she gave birth to her firstborn son, and she wrapped him tightly in cloth and laid him in a manger, because there was no guest room available for them.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 10,\n      \"text\": \"But the angel said to them, \\\"Don't be afraid, for look, I proclaim to you good news of great joy that will be for all the people:\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 11,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"Today in the city of David a Savior was born for you, who is the Messiah, the Lord.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 12,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"This will be the sign for you: You will find a baby wrapped tightly in cloth and lying in a manger.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 13,\n      \"text\": \"Suddenly there was a multitude of the heavenly host with the angel, praising God and saying:\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 14,\n      \"text\": \"Glory to God in the highest heaven, and peace on earth to people he favors!\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 19,\n      \"text\": \"But Mary was treasuring up all these things in her heart and meditating on them.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"luk\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 2\n}\n```\n\n## Luke 2:10-11 (CSB)\n\n### Good tidings of great joy\n\nBut the angel said to them, \"Don't be afraid, for look, I proclaim to you good news of great joy that will be for all the people: \"Today in the city of David a Savior was born for you, who is the Messiah, the Lord.\n\n*Tags: nativity, joy*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-08\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Luke 2:1-20\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Read the birth, the angel's message, the shepherds' visit, and Mary's pondering as one narrative. The announcement identifies the child as Savior, Messiah, and Lord; the shepherds then go to see him.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Luke 2:6-7, 10-14, 19 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 6,\n      \"text\": \"While they were there, the time came for her to give birth.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 7,\n      \"text\": \"Then she gave birth to her firstborn son, and she wrapped him tightly in cloth and laid him in a manger, because there was no guest room available for them.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 10,\n      \"text\": \"But the angel said to them, \\\"Don't be afraid, for look, I proclaim to you good news of great joy that will be for all the people:\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 11,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"Today in the city of David a Savior was born for you, who is the Messiah, the Lord.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 12,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"This will be the sign for you: You will find a baby wrapped tightly in cloth and lying in a manger.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 13,\n      \"text\": \"Suddenly there was a multitude of the heavenly host with the angel, praising God and saying:\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 14,\n      \"text\": \"Glory to God in the highest heaven, and peace on earth to people he favors!\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 19,\n      \"text\": \"But Mary was treasuring up all these things in her heart and meditating on them.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"luk\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 2\n}\n```\n\n## Luke 2:13-14 (CSB)\n\n### Glory to God in the highest\n\nSuddenly there was a multitude of the heavenly host with the angel, praising God and saying: Glory to God in the highest heaven, and peace on earth to people he favors!\n\n*Tags: peace, joy*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-09\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Luke 2:1-20\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Read the birth, the angel's message, the shepherds' visit, and Mary's pondering as one narrative. The announcement identifies the child as Savior, Messiah, and Lord; the shepherds then go to see him.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Luke 2:6-7, 10-14, 19 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 6,\n      \"text\": \"While they were there, the time came for her to give birth.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 7,\n      \"text\": \"Then she gave birth to her firstborn son, and she wrapped him tightly in cloth and laid him in a manger, because there was no guest room available for them.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 10,\n      \"text\": \"But the angel said to them, \\\"Don't be afraid, for look, I proclaim to you good news of great joy that will be for all the people:\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 11,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"Today in the city of David a Savior was born for you, who is the Messiah, the Lord.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 12,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"This will be the sign for you: You will find a baby wrapped tightly in cloth and lying in a manger.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 13,\n      \"text\": \"Suddenly there was a multitude of the heavenly host with the angel, praising God and saying:\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 14,\n      \"text\": \"Glory to God in the highest heaven, and peace on earth to people he favors!\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 19,\n      \"text\": \"But Mary was treasuring up all these things in her heart and meditating on them.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"luk\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 2\n}\n```\n\n## Luke 2:19 (CSB)\n\n### Mary treasured these things\n\nBut Mary was treasuring up all these things in her heart and meditating on them.\n\n*Tags: wonder, mary*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-10\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Luke 2:1-20\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Read the birth, the angel's message, the shepherds' visit, and Mary's pondering as one narrative. The announcement identifies the child as Savior, Messiah, and Lord; the shepherds then go to see him.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Luke 2:6-7, 10-14, 19 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 6,\n      \"text\": \"While they were there, the time came for her to give birth.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 7,\n      \"text\": \"Then she gave birth to her firstborn son, and she wrapped him tightly in cloth and laid him in a manger, because there was no guest room available for them.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 10,\n      \"text\": \"But the angel said to them, \\\"Don't be afraid, for look, I proclaim to you good news of great joy that will be for all the people:\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 11,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"Today in the city of David a Savior was born for you, who is the Messiah, the Lord.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 12,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"This will be the sign for you: You will find a baby wrapped tightly in cloth and lying in a manger.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 13,\n      \"text\": \"Suddenly there was a multitude of the heavenly host with the angel, praising God and saying:\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 14,\n      \"text\": \"Glory to God in the highest heaven, and peace on earth to people he favors!\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 19,\n      \"text\": \"But Mary was treasuring up all these things in her heart and meditating on them.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"luk\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 2\n}\n```\n\n## Matthew 2:10-11 (CSB)\n\n### They rejoiced with great joy\n\nWhen they saw the star, they were overwhelmed with joy. Entering the house, they saw the child with Mary his mother, and falling to their knees, they worshiped him. Then they opened their treasures and presented him with gifts: gold, frankincense, and myrrh.\n\n*Tags: star, gifts*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-11\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Matthew 2:1-12\",\n  \"context_note\": \"The visitors seek the king, encounter Herod, and worship Jesus in a house. Matthew does not place this visit at the manger on the birth night. The gifts belong to their worship and the larger contrast between their response and Herod's.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Matthew 2:9-12 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 9,\n      \"text\": \"After hearing the king, they went on their way. And there it was -- the star they had seen at its rising. It led them until it came and stopped above the place where the child was.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 10,\n      \"text\": \"When they saw the star, they were overwhelmed with joy.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 11,\n      \"text\": \"Entering the house, they saw the child with Mary his mother, and falling to their knees, they worshiped him. Then they opened their treasures and presented him with gifts: gold, frankincense, and myrrh.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 12,\n      \"text\": \"And being warned in a dream not to go back to Herod, they returned to their own country by another route.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"mat\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 2\n}\n```\n\n## John 1:14 (CSB)\n\n### The Word became flesh\n\nThe Word became flesh and dwelt among us. We observed his glory, the glory as the one and only Son from the Father, full of grace and truth.\n\n*Tags: incarnation, grace*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-12\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"John 1:1-18\",\n  \"context_note\": \"The Word who becomes flesh is the Word already described as with God, as God, and as active in creation. His coming reveals the Father and brings grace and truth; it is more than a general image of kindness.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"John 1:14-18 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 14,\n      \"text\": \"The Word became flesh and dwelt among us. We observed his glory, the glory as the one and only Son from the Father, full of grace and truth.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 15,\n      \"text\": \"(John testified concerning him and exclaimed, \\\"This was the one of whom I said, 'The one coming after me ranks ahead of me, because he existed before me.' \\\")\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 16,\n      \"text\": \"Indeed, we have all received grace upon grace from his fullness,\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 17,\n      \"text\": \"for the law was given through Moses; grace and truth came through Jesus Christ.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 18,\n      \"text\": \"No one has ever seen God. The one and only Son, who is himself God and is at the Father's side -- he has revealed him.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"jhn\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 1\n}\n```\n\n## John 3:16 (CSB)\n\n### For God so loved the world\n\n\"For God loved the world in this way: He gave his one and only Son, so that everyone who believes in him will not perish but have eternal life.\n\n*Tags: love, gift*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-13\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"John 3:1-21\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Jesus speaks with Nicodemus about new birth, the Spirit, the lifting up of the Son of Man, and faith. God's gift and eternal life sit alongside the passage's account of judgment, light, and human response.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"John 3:5-8, 16 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 5,\n      \"text\": \"Jesus answered, \\\"Truly I tell you, unless someone is born of water and the Spirit, he cannot enter the kingdom of God.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 6,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"Whatever is born of the flesh is flesh, and whatever is born of the Spirit is spirit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 7,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"Do not be amazed that I told you that you must be born again.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 8,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"The wind blows where it pleases, and you hear its sound, but you don't know where it comes from or where it is going. So it is with everyone born of the Spirit.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 16,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"For God loved the world in this way: He gave his one and only Son, so that everyone who believes in him will not perish but have eternal life.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"jhn\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 3\n}\n```\n\n## James 1:17 (CSB)\n\n### Every good and perfect gift\n\nEvery good and perfect gift is from above, coming down from the Father of lights, who does not change like shifting shadows.\n\n*Tags: gift, gratitude*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-14\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"James 1:12-27\",\n  \"context_note\": \"James distinguishes temptation from God's good gifts, then calls readers to hear and do the word. Care for vulnerable people belongs with disciplined speech and a life unstained by the world.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"James 1:17, 27 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 17,\n      \"text\": \"Every good and perfect gift is from above, coming down from the Father of lights, who does not change like shifting shadows.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 27,\n      \"text\": \"Pure and undefiled religion before God the Father is this: to look after orphans and widows in their distress and to keep oneself unstained from the world.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"jas\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 1\n}\n```\n\n## 2 Corinthians 9:15 (CSB)\n\n### His indescribable gift\n\nThanks be to God for his indescribable gift!\n\n*Tags: gift, gratitude*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-15\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"2 Corinthians 9:6-15\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Paul encourages willing, cheerful generosity in a collection for others. God's provision produces both practical help and thanksgiving; the closing thanks should be read within that whole movement of grace and giving.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"2 Corinthians 9:12-15 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 12,\n      \"text\": \"For the ministry of this service is not only supplying the needs of the saints but is also overflowing in many expressions of thanks to God.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 13,\n      \"text\": \"Because of the proof provided by this ministry, they will glorify God for your obedient confession of the gospel of Christ, and for your generosity in sharing with them and with everyone.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 14,\n      \"text\": \"And as they pray on your behalf, they will have deep affection for you because of the surpassing grace of God in you.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 15,\n      \"text\": \"Thanks be to God for his indescribable gift!\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"2co\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 9\n}\n```\n\n## 1 John 4:9 (CSB)\n\n### God sent his only Son\n\nGod's love was revealed among us in this way: God sent his one and only Son into the world so that we might live through him.\n\n*Tags: love, life*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-16\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"1 John 4:7-21\",\n  \"context_note\": \"John grounds love for one another in God's prior love, the sending of his Son, and Christ's saving work. The passage connects confession of Jesus, abiding in God, and concrete love of a brother or sister.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"1 John 4:7-11 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 7,\n      \"text\": \"Dear friends, let us love one another, because love is from God, and everyone who loves has been born of God and knows God.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 8,\n      \"text\": \"The one who does not love does not know God, because God is love.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 9,\n      \"text\": \"God's love was revealed among us in this way: God sent his one and only Son into the world so that we might live through him.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 10,\n      \"text\": \"Love consists in this: not that we loved God, but that he loved us and sent his Son to be the atoning sacrifice for our sins.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 11,\n      \"text\": \"Dear friends, if God loved us in this way, we also must love one another.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"1jo\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 4\n}\n```\n\n## Matthew 11:28-30 (CSB)\n\n### Come to the humble King\n\n\"Come to me, all of you who are weary and burdened, and I will give you rest. \"Take my yoke upon you and learn from me, because I am lowly and humble in heart, and you will find rest for your souls. \"For my yoke is easy and my burden is light.\"\n\n*Tags: grace, rest, burden*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-quest-1\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Matthew 11:25-30\",\n  \"context_note\": \"The invitation follows Jesus' words about knowing and revealing the Father. His rest includes coming to him, learning from him, and taking his gentle yoke: a call to discipleship with the humble Son.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Matthew 11:27-30 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 27,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"All things have been entrusted to me by my Father. No one knows the Son except the Father, and no one knows the Father except the Son and anyone to whom the Son desires to reveal him.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 28,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"Come to me, all of you who are weary and burdened, and I will give you rest.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 29,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"Take my yoke upon you and learn from me, because I am lowly and humble in heart, and you will find rest for your souls.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 30,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"For my yoke is easy and my burden is light.\\\"\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"mat\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 11\n}\n```\n\n## Mark 10:45 (CSB)\n\n### The King who serves\n\n\"For even the Son of Man did not come to be served, but to serve, and to give his life as a ransom for many.\"\n\n*Tags: Christ, service, gospel*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-quest-2\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Mark 10:35-45\",\n  \"context_note\": \"James and John ask for places of honor. Jesus contrasts rulers who dominate with greatness expressed in service, then names his own unique mission of giving his life as a ransom.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Mark 10:42-45 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 42,\n      \"text\": \"Jesus called them over and said to them, \\\"You know that those who are regarded as rulers of the Gentiles lord it over them, and those in high positions act as tyrants over them.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 43,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"But it is not so among you. On the contrary, whoever wants to become great among you will be your servant,\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 44,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"and whoever wants to be first among you will be a slave to all.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 45,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"For even the Son of Man did not come to be served, but to serve, and to give his life as a ransom for many.\\\"\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"mar\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 10\n}\n```\n\n## Ephesians 2:8-10 (CSB)\n\n### Saved by grace, created for good works\n\nFor you are saved by grace through faith, and this is not from yourselves; it is God's gift -- not from works, so that no one can boast. For we are his workmanship, created in Christ Jesus for good works, which God prepared ahead of time for us to do.\n\n*Tags: grace, faith, gift, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-quest-3\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Ephesians 2:1-10\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Paul first describes death in sin and God's act of making people alive with Christ. Grace and faith come before the good works of verse 10: those works are the purpose and fruit of the new life, not its purchase price.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Ephesians 2:4-10 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 4,\n      \"text\": \"But God, who is rich in mercy, because of his great love that he had for us,\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 5,\n      \"text\": \"made us alive with Christ even though we were dead in trespasses. You are saved by grace!\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 6,\n      \"text\": \"He also raised us up with him and seated us with him in the heavens in Christ Jesus,\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 7,\n      \"text\": \"so that in the coming ages he might display the immeasurable riches of his grace through his kindness to us in Christ Jesus.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 8,\n      \"text\": \"For you are saved by grace through faith, and this is not from yourselves; it is God's gift --\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 9,\n      \"text\": \"not from works, so that no one can boast.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 10,\n      \"text\": \"For we are his workmanship, created in Christ Jesus for good works, which God prepared ahead of time for us to do.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"eph\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 2\n}\n```\n\n## 1 Corinthians 15:3-4 (CSB)\n\n### Christ died and rose again\n\nFor I passed on to you as most important what I also received: that Christ died for our sins according to the Scriptures, that he was buried, that he was raised on the third day according to the Scriptures,\n\n*Tags: gospel, resurrection, Christ*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-quest-4\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"1 Corinthians 15:1-11\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Paul reminds the church of the gospel they received and the witnesses to Christ's resurrection. Death, burial, resurrection, appearances, and God's grace belong together in his argument.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"1 Corinthians 15:3-8 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 3,\n      \"text\": \"For I passed on to you as most important what I also received: that Christ died for our sins according to the Scriptures,\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 4,\n      \"text\": \"that he was buried, that he was raised on the third day according to the Scriptures,\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 5,\n      \"text\": \"and that he appeared to Cephas, then to the Twelve.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 6,\n      \"text\": \"Then he appeared to over five hundred brothers and sisters at one time; most of them are still alive, but some have fallen asleep.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 7,\n      \"text\": \"Then he appeared to James, then to all the apostles.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 8,\n      \"text\": \"Last of all, as to one born at the wrong time, he also appeared to me.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"1co\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 15\n}\n```\n\n## James 1:27 (CSB)\n\n### Visit the fatherless and widows\n\nPure and undefiled religion before God the Father is this: to look after orphans and widows in their distress and to keep oneself unstained from the world.\n\n*Tags: widow, orphan, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-quest-5\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"James 1:12-27\",\n  \"context_note\": \"James distinguishes temptation from God's good gifts, then calls readers to hear and do the word. Care for vulnerable people belongs with disciplined speech and a life unstained by the world.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"James 1:17, 27 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 17,\n      \"text\": \"Every good and perfect gift is from above, coming down from the Father of lights, who does not change like shifting shadows.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 27,\n      \"text\": \"Pure and undefiled religion before God the Father is this: to look after orphans and widows in their distress and to keep oneself unstained from the world.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"jas\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 1\n}\n```\n\n## Leviticus 19:33-34 (CSB)\n\n### Love the stranger as yourself\n\n\"When an alien resides with you in your land, you must not oppress him. \"You will regard the alien who resides with you as the native-born among you. You are to love him as yourself, for you were aliens in the land of Egypt; I am the LORD your God.\n\n*Tags: stranger, neighbor, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-quest-6\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Leviticus 19:1-37\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Israel's call to holiness includes honest judgment, care for the poor, love of neighbor, and fair treatment of the resident foreigner. Remembering their own life in Egypt shapes how they must treat those living among them.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Leviticus 19:18, 33-34 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 18,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"Do not take revenge or bear a grudge against members of your community, but love your neighbor as yourself; I am the LORD.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 33,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"When an alien resides with you in your land, you must not oppress him.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 34,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"You will regard the alien who resides with you as the native-born among you. You are to love him as yourself, for you were aliens in the land of Egypt; I am the LORD your God.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"lev\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 19\n}\n```\n\n## Galatians 5:13-14 (CSB)\n\n### By love serve one another\n\nFor you were called to be free, brothers and sisters; only don't use this freedom as an opportunity for the flesh, but serve one another through love. For the whole law is fulfilled in one statement: Love your neighbor as yourself.\n\n*Tags: love, freedom, service*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-quest-7\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Galatians 5:1-26\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Paul defends freedom in Christ and rejects reliance on circumcision for justification. That freedom is expressed through faith working in love and walking by the Spirit, rather than self-indulgence or hostility.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Galatians 5:6, 13-14, 22-23 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 6,\n      \"text\": \"For in Christ Jesus neither circumcision nor uncircumcision accomplishes anything; what matters is faith working through love.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 13,\n      \"text\": \"For you were called to be free, brothers and sisters; only don't use this freedom as an opportunity for the flesh, but serve one another through love.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 14,\n      \"text\": \"For the whole law is fulfilled in one statement: Love your neighbor as yourself.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 22,\n      \"text\": \"But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness,\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 23,\n      \"text\": \"gentleness, and self-control. The law is not against such things.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"gal\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 5\n}\n```\n\n## Luke 2:12 (CSB)\n\n### The sign of the manger\n\n\"This will be the sign for you: You will find a baby wrapped tightly in cloth and lying in a manger.\"\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-24\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Luke 2:1-20\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Read the birth, the angel's message, the shepherds' visit, and Mary's pondering as one narrative. The announcement identifies the child as Savior, Messiah, and Lord; the shepherds then go to see him.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Luke 2:6-7, 10-14, 19 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 6,\n      \"text\": \"While they were there, the time came for her to give birth.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 7,\n      \"text\": \"Then she gave birth to her firstborn son, and she wrapped him tightly in cloth and laid him in a manger, because there was no guest room available for them.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 10,\n      \"text\": \"But the angel said to them, \\\"Don't be afraid, for look, I proclaim to you good news of great joy that will be for all the people:\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 11,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"Today in the city of David a Savior was born for you, who is the Messiah, the Lord.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 12,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"This will be the sign for you: You will find a baby wrapped tightly in cloth and lying in a manger.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 13,\n      \"text\": \"Suddenly there was a multitude of the heavenly host with the angel, praising God and saying:\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 14,\n      \"text\": \"Glory to God in the highest heaven, and peace on earth to people he favors!\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 19,\n      \"text\": \"But Mary was treasuring up all these things in her heart and meditating on them.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"luk\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 2\n}\n```\n\n## John 3:5-8 (CSB)\n\n### Born of the Spirit\n\nJesus answered, \"Truly I tell you, unless someone is born of water and the Spirit, he cannot enter the kingdom of God. \"Whatever is born of the flesh is flesh, and whatever is born of the Spirit is spirit. \"Do not be amazed that I told you that you must be born again. \"The wind blows where it pleases, and you hear its sound, but you don't know where it comes from or where it is going. So it is with everyone born of the Spirit.\"\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-25\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"John 3:1-21\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Jesus speaks with Nicodemus about new birth, the Spirit, the lifting up of the Son of Man, and faith. God's gift and eternal life sit alongside the passage's account of judgment, light, and human response.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"John 3:5-8, 16 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 5,\n      \"text\": \"Jesus answered, \\\"Truly I tell you, unless someone is born of water and the Spirit, he cannot enter the kingdom of God.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 6,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"Whatever is born of the flesh is flesh, and whatever is born of the Spirit is spirit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 7,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"Do not be amazed that I told you that you must be born again.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 8,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"The wind blows where it pleases, and you hear its sound, but you don't know where it comes from or where it is going. So it is with everyone born of the Spirit.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 16,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"For God loved the world in this way: He gave his one and only Son, so that everyone who believes in him will not perish but have eternal life.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"jhn\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 3\n}\n```\n\n## Galatians 5:6 (CSB)\n\n### Faith working through love\n\nFor in Christ Jesus neither circumcision nor uncircumcision accomplishes anything; what matters is faith working through love.\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-26\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Galatians 5:1-26\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Paul defends freedom in Christ and rejects reliance on circumcision for justification. That freedom is expressed through faith working in love and walking by the Spirit, rather than self-indulgence or hostility.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Galatians 5:6, 13-14, 22-23 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 6,\n      \"text\": \"For in Christ Jesus neither circumcision nor uncircumcision accomplishes anything; what matters is faith working through love.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 13,\n      \"text\": \"For you were called to be free, brothers and sisters; only don't use this freedom as an opportunity for the flesh, but serve one another through love.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 14,\n      \"text\": \"For the whole law is fulfilled in one statement: Love your neighbor as yourself.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 22,\n      \"text\": \"But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness,\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 23,\n      \"text\": \"gentleness, and self-control. The law is not against such things.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"gal\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 5\n}\n```\n\n## Galatians 5:22-23 (CSB)\n\n### The fruit of the Spirit\n\nBut the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness, and self-control. The law is not against such things.\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-27\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Galatians 5:1-26\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Paul defends freedom in Christ and rejects reliance on circumcision for justification. That freedom is expressed through faith working in love and walking by the Spirit, rather than self-indulgence or hostility.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Galatians 5:6, 13-14, 22-23 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 6,\n      \"text\": \"For in Christ Jesus neither circumcision nor uncircumcision accomplishes anything; what matters is faith working through love.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 13,\n      \"text\": \"For you were called to be free, brothers and sisters; only don't use this freedom as an opportunity for the flesh, but serve one another through love.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 14,\n      \"text\": \"For the whole law is fulfilled in one statement: Love your neighbor as yourself.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 22,\n      \"text\": \"But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness,\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 23,\n      \"text\": \"gentleness, and self-control. The law is not against such things.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"gal\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 5\n}\n```\n\n## Luke 19:1-10 (CSB)\n\n### The Son of Man seeks the lost\n\nHe entered Jericho and was passing through. There was a man named Zacchaeus who was a chief tax collector, and he was rich. He was trying to see who Jesus was, but he was not able because of the crowd, since he was a short man. So running ahead, he climbed up a sycamore tree to see Jesus, since he was about to pass that way. When Jesus came to the place, he looked up and said to him, \"Zacchaeus, hurry and come down because today it is necessary for me to stay at your house.\" So he quickly came down and welcomed him joyfully. All who saw it began to complain, \"He's gone to stay with a sinful man.\" But Zacchaeus stood there and said to the Lord, \"Look, I'll give half of my possessions to the poor, Lord. And if I have extorted anything from anyone, I'll pay back four times as much.\" \"Today salvation has come to this house,\" Jesus told him, \"because he too is a son of Abraham. \"For the Son of Man has come to seek and to save the lost.\"\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-28\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Luke 18:35-19:10\",\n  \"context_note\": \"The approach to Jericho leads from a blind man's plea to Jesus' welcome of Zacchaeus. Zacchaeus responds with generosity and restitution; Jesus' saving initiative is not something Zacchaeus buys with his money.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Luke 19:1-10 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"He entered Jericho and was passing through.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 2,\n      \"text\": \"There was a man named Zacchaeus who was a chief tax collector, and he was rich.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 3,\n      \"text\": \"He was trying to see who Jesus was, but he was not able because of the crowd, since he was a short man.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 4,\n      \"text\": \"So running ahead, he climbed up a sycamore tree to see Jesus, since he was about to pass that way.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 5,\n      \"text\": \"When Jesus came to the place, he looked up and said to him, \\\"Zacchaeus, hurry and come down because today it is necessary for me to stay at your house.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 6,\n      \"text\": \"So he quickly came down and welcomed him joyfully.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 7,\n      \"text\": \"All who saw it began to complain, \\\"He's gone to stay with a sinful man.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 8,\n      \"text\": \"But Zacchaeus stood there and said to the Lord, \\\"Look, I'll give half of my possessions to the poor, Lord. And if I have extorted anything from anyone, I'll pay back four times as much.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 9,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"Today salvation has come to this house,\\\" Jesus told him, \\\"because he too is a son of Abraham.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 10,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"For the Son of Man has come to seek and to save the lost.\\\"\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"luk\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 19\n}\n```\n\n## John 16:13-14 (CSB)\n\n### The Spirit glorifies Jesus\n\n\"When the Spirit of truth comes, he will guide you into all the truth. For he will not speak on his own, but he will speak whatever he hears. He will also declare to you what is to come. \"He will glorify me, because he will take from what is mine and declare it to you.\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-29\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"John 16:1-15\",\n  \"context_note\": \"These words belong to Jesus' farewell teaching to his disciples as they face his departure and opposition. The Spirit's work centers on truth and glorifying Jesus; read that audience and purpose before applying the promise.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"John 16:12-15 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 12,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"I still have many things to tell you, but you can't bear them now.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 13,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"When the Spirit of truth comes, he will guide you into all the truth. For he will not speak on his own, but he will speak whatever he hears. He will also declare to you what is to come.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 14,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"He will glorify me, because he will take from what is mine and declare it to you.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 15,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"Everything the Father has is mine. This is why I told you that he takes from what is mine and will declare it to you.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"jhn\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 16\n}\n```\n\n## Titus 3:4-7 (CSB)\n\n### Saved according to his mercy\n\nBut when the kindness of God our Savior and his love for mankind appeared, he saved us -- not by works of righteousness that we had done, but according to his mercy -- through the washing of regeneration and renewal by the Holy Spirit. He poured out his Spirit on us abundantly through Jesus Christ our Savior so that, having been justified by his grace, we may become heirs with the hope of eternal life.\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-30\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Titus 3:1-8\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Paul recalls former foolishness and God's merciful rescue, then urges believers toward good works. The passage holds justification, renewal by the Holy Spirit, hope, and a changed public life together.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Titus 3:3-8 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 3,\n      \"text\": \"For we too were once foolish, disobedient, deceived, enslaved by various passions and pleasures, living in malice and envy, hateful, detesting one another.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 4,\n      \"text\": \"But when the kindness of God our Savior and his love for mankind appeared,\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 5,\n      \"text\": \"he saved us -- not by works of righteousness that we had done, but according to his mercy -- through the washing of regeneration and renewal by the Holy Spirit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 6,\n      \"text\": \"He poured out his Spirit on us abundantly through Jesus Christ our Savior\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 7,\n      \"text\": \"so that, having been justified by his grace, we may become heirs with the hope of eternal life.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 8,\n      \"text\": \"This saying is trustworthy. I want you to insist on these things, so that those who have believed God might be careful to devote themselves to good works. These are good and profitable for everyone.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"tit\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 3\n}\n```\n\n## 1 John 3:16-18 (CSB)\n\n### Love in action and truth\n\nThis is how we have come to know love: He laid down his life for us. We should also lay down our lives for our brothers and sisters. If anyone has this world's goods and sees a fellow believer in need but withholds compassion from him -- how does God's love reside in him? Little children, let us not love in word or speech, but in action and in truth.\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-31\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"1 John 3:11-24\",\n  \"context_note\": \"John contrasts hatred with the love shown in Jesus laying down his life. Love in action includes sharing material goods with a fellow believer in need, within the larger call to faith in Christ and love for one another.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"1 John 3:16-20 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 16,\n      \"text\": \"This is how we have come to know love: He laid down his life for us. We should also lay down our lives for our brothers and sisters.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 17,\n      \"text\": \"If anyone has this world's goods and sees a fellow believer in need but withholds compassion from him -- how does God's love reside in him?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 18,\n      \"text\": \"Little children, let us not love in word or speech, but in action and in truth.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 19,\n      \"text\": \"This is how we will know that we belong to the truth and will reassure our hearts before him\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 20,\n      \"text\": \"whenever our hearts condemn us; for God is greater than our hearts, and he knows all things.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"1jo\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 3\n}\n```\n\n## Hebrews 13:1-2 (CSB)\n\n### Welcome one another\n\nLet brotherly love continue. Don't neglect to show hospitality, for by doing this some have welcomed angels as guests without knowing it.\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-32\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Hebrews 13:1-6\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Hospitality appears among connected instructions about love, prisoners, marriage, contentment, and confidence in God's presence. The mention of angels encourages welcoming strangers, rather than turning guests into a guessing game.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Hebrews 13:1-3 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"Let brotherly love continue.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 2,\n      \"text\": \"Don't neglect to show hospitality, for by doing this some have welcomed angels as guests without knowing it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 3,\n      \"text\": \"Remember those in prison, as though you were in prison with them, and the mistreated, as though you yourselves were suffering bodily.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"heb\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 13\n}\n```\n\n## James 2:14-17 (CSB)\n\n### Living faith acts\n\nWhat good is it, my brothers and sisters, if someone claims to have faith but does not have works? Can such faith save him? If a brother or sister is without clothes and lacks daily food and one of you says to them, \"Go in peace, stay warm, and be well fed,\" but you don't give them what the body needs, what good is it? In the same way faith, if it does not have works, is dead by itself.\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-33\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"James 2:1-26\",\n  \"context_note\": \"James confronts favoritism and a claim to faith that refuses practical help. Read the example of the hungry neighbor within his argument that living faith acts; empty assurances do not feed or clothe anyone.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"James 2:14-18 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 14,\n      \"text\": \"What good is it, my brothers and sisters, if someone claims to have faith but does not have works? Can such faith save him?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 15,\n      \"text\": \"If a brother or sister is without clothes and lacks daily food\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 16,\n      \"text\": \"and one of you says to them, \\\"Go in peace, stay warm, and be well fed,\\\" but you don't give them what the body needs, what good is it?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 17,\n      \"text\": \"In the same way faith, if it does not have works, is dead by itself.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 18,\n      \"text\": \"But someone will say, \\\"You have faith, and I have works.\\\" Show me your faith without works, and I will show you faith by my works.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"jas\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 2\n}\n```\n\n## Matthew 25:35-40 (CSB)\n\n### The King and the least of his family\n\n\" 'For I was hungry and you gave me something to eat; I was thirsty and you gave me something to drink; I was a stranger and you took me in; \"I was naked and you clothed me; I was sick and you took care of me; I was in prison and you visited me.' \"Then the righteous will answer him, 'Lord, when did we see you hungry and feed you, or thirsty and give you something to drink? \"When did we see you a stranger and take you in, or without clothes and clothe you? \"When did we see you sick, or in prison, and visit you? ' \"And the King will answer them, 'Truly I tell you, whatever you did for one of the least of these brothers and sisters of mine, you did for me.'\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-34\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Matthew 25:31-46\",\n  \"context_note\": \"The Son of Man judges the nations and identifies with the least of his brothers and sisters. Read the full scene, its audience, and both responses before turning selected acts into a detached checklist.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Matthew 25:31-40 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 31,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"When the Son of Man comes in his glory, and all the angels with him, then he will sit on his glorious throne.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 32,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"All the nations will be gathered before him, and he will separate them one from another, just as a shepherd separates the sheep from the goats.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 33,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"He will put the sheep on his right and the goats on the left.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 34,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"Then the King will say to those on his right, 'Come, you who are blessed by my Father; inherit the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 35,\n      \"text\": \"\\\" 'For I was hungry and you gave me something to eat; I was thirsty and you gave me something to drink; I was a stranger and you took me in;\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 36,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"I was naked and you clothed me; I was sick and you took care of me; I was in prison and you visited me.'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 37,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"Then the righteous will answer him, 'Lord, when did we see you hungry and feed you, or thirsty and give you something to drink?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 38,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"When did we see you a stranger and take you in, or without clothes and clothe you?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 39,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"When did we see you sick, or in prison, and visit you? '\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 40,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"And the King will answer them, 'Truly I tell you, whatever you did for one of the least of these brothers and sisters of mine, you did for me.'\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"mat\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 25\n}\n```\n\n## Romans 12:15 (CSB)\n\n### Rejoice and weep together\n\nRejoice with those who rejoice; weep with those who weep.\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-35\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Romans 12:1-21\",\n  \"context_note\": \"The chapter begins with God's mercies and a life offered to him. Rejoicing and weeping with others belong among sincere love, hospitality, blessing opponents, and refusing revenge.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Romans 12:13-16 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 13,\n      \"text\": \"Share with the saints in their needs; pursue hospitality.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 14,\n      \"text\": \"Bless those who persecute you; bless and do not curse.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 15,\n      \"text\": \"Rejoice with those who rejoice; weep with those who weep.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 16,\n      \"text\": \"Live in harmony with one another. Do not be proud; instead, associate with the humble. Do not be wise in your own estimation.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"rom\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 12\n}\n```\n\n## Psalm 34:18 (CSB)\n\n### Near to the brokenhearted\n\nThe LORD is near the brokenhearted; he saves those crushed in spirit.\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-36\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Psalm 34:15-22\",\n  \"context_note\": \"The psalm speaks both of God's nearness and of the righteous person's many afflictions. Comfort here does not mean that grief or trouble is unreal; the surrounding lines place suffering within dependence on the Lord.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Psalm 34:17-19 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 17,\n      \"text\": \"The righteous cry out, and the LORD hears, and rescues them from all their troubles.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 18,\n      \"text\": \"The LORD is near the brokenhearted; he saves those crushed in spirit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 19,\n      \"text\": \"One who is righteous has many adversities, but the LORD rescues him from them all.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"psa\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 34\n}\n```\n\n## Deuteronomy 10:18-19 (CSB)\n\n### Love the resident foreigner\n\n\"He executes justice for the fatherless and the widow, and loves the resident alien, giving him food and clothing. \"You are also to love the resident alien, since you were resident aliens in the land of Egypt.\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-37\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Deuteronomy 10:12-22\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Israel is called to fear, love, and serve the Lord, whose greatness includes justice for the fatherless, widow, and resident foreigner. Their own experience in Egypt grounds the command to love the foreigner.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Deuteronomy 10:17-19 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 17,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"For the LORD your God is the God of gods and Lord of lords, the great, mighty, and awe-inspiring God, showing no partiality and taking no bribe.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 18,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"He executes justice for the fatherless and the widow, and loves the resident alien, giving him food and clothing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 19,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"You are also to love the resident alien, since you were resident aliens in the land of Egypt.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"deu\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 10\n}\n```\n\n## Genesis 1:27 (CSB)\n\n### Made in God’s image\n\nSo God created man in his own image; he created him in the image of God; he created them male and female.\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-38\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Genesis 1:26-31\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Human beings, male and female, are made in God's image, blessed, and entrusted with a place and task in his creation. Read human dignity together with that blessing and responsibility.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Genesis 1:26-28 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 26,\n      \"text\": \"Then God said, \\\"Let us make man in our image, according to our likeness. They will rule the fish of the sea, the birds of the sky, the livestock, the whole earth, and the creatures that crawl on the earth.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 27,\n      \"text\": \"So God created man in his own image; he created him in the image of God; he created them male and female.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 28,\n      \"text\": \"God blessed them, and God said to them, \\\"Be fruitful, multiply, fill the earth, and subdue it. Rule the fish of the sea, the birds of the sky, and every creature that crawls on the earth.\\\"\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"gen\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 1\n}\n```\n\n## Colossians 3:17 (CSB)\n\n### Everything in the name of Jesus\n\nAnd whatever you do, in word or in deed, do everything in the name of the Lord Jesus, giving thanks to God the Father through him.\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-39\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Colossians 3:1-17\",\n  \"context_note\": \"The command to do everything in Jesus' name follows putting off the old life and putting on compassion, forgiveness, and love. Christ's peace, his word, and thanksgiving shape what that life looks like.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Colossians 3:15-17 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 15,\n      \"text\": \"And let the peace of Christ, to which you were also called in one body, rule your hearts. And be thankful.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 16,\n      \"text\": \"Let the word of Christ dwell richly among you, in all wisdom teaching and admonishing one another through psalms, hymns, and spiritual songs, singing to God with gratitude in your hearts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 17,\n      \"text\": \"And whatever you do, in word or in deed, do everything in the name of the Lord Jesus, giving thanks to God the Father through him.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"col\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 3\n}\n```\n\n## Galatians 2:20 (CSB)\n\n### Christ lives in me\n\nI have been crucified with Christ, and I no longer live, but Christ lives in me. The life I now live in the body, I live by faith in the Son of God, who loved me and gave himself for me.\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-40\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Galatians 2:15-21\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Paul's words about life with Christ belong to his argument about justification through faith in Christ rather than works of the law. His personal language rests on Christ's love and self-giving, not self-improvement alone.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Galatians 2:19-21 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 19,\n      \"text\": \"For through the law I died to the law, so that I might live for God.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 20,\n      \"text\": \"I have been crucified with Christ, and I no longer live, but Christ lives in me. The life I now live in the body, I live by faith in the Son of God, who loved me and gave himself for me.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 21,\n      \"text\": \"I do not set aside the grace of God, for if righteousness comes through the law, then Christ died for nothing.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"gal\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 2\n}\n```\n\n## John 11:25-26 (CSB)\n\n### The resurrection and the life\n\nJesus said to her, \"I am the resurrection and the life. The one who believes in me, even if he dies, will live. \"Everyone who lives and believes in me will never die. Do you believe this? \"\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-41\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"John 11:17-44\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Jesus meets Martha and Mary in their grief before calling Lazarus from the tomb. His claim to be resurrection and life, the sisters' responses, his tears, and the sign itself belong in the same account.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"John 11:25-26, 35 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 25,\n      \"text\": \"Jesus said to her, \\\"I am the resurrection and the life. The one who believes in me, even if he dies, will live.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 26,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"Everyone who lives and believes in me will never die. Do you believe this? \\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 35,\n      \"text\": \"Jesus wept.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"jhn\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 11\n}\n```\n\n## John 11:35 (CSB)\n\n### Jesus wept\n\nJesus wept.\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-42\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"John 11:17-44\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Jesus meets Martha and Mary in their grief before calling Lazarus from the tomb. His claim to be resurrection and life, the sisters' responses, his tears, and the sign itself belong in the same account.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"John 11:25-26, 35 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 25,\n      \"text\": \"Jesus said to her, \\\"I am the resurrection and the life. The one who believes in me, even if he dies, will live.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 26,\n      \"text\": \"\\\"Everyone who lives and believes in me will never die. Do you believe this? \\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 35,\n      \"text\": \"Jesus wept.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"jhn\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 11\n}\n```\n\n## 1 Peter 1:3 (CSB)\n\n### New birth into a living hope\n\nBlessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ. Because of his great mercy he has given us new birth into a living hope through the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-43\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"1 Peter 1:3-9\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Peter blesses God for new birth and living hope through Jesus' resurrection, while acknowledging present grief in trials. Hope and rejoicing are grounded in salvation, not in pretending that suffering has disappeared.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"1 Peter 1:3-5 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 3,\n      \"text\": \"Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ. Because of his great mercy he has given us new birth into a living hope through the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 4,\n      \"text\": \"and into an inheritance that is imperishable, undefiled, and unfading, kept in heaven for you.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 5,\n      \"text\": \"You are being guarded by God's power through faith for a salvation that is ready to be revealed in the last time.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"1pe\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 1\n}\n```\n\n## 1 Peter 2:24 (CSB)\n\n### He bore our sins\n\nHe himself bore our sins in his body on the tree; so that, having died to sins, we might live for righteousness. By his wounds you have been healed.\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-44\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"1 Peter 2:18-25\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Peter addresses enslaved people suffering unjustly and points to Christ's suffering and sin-bearing. The healing language belongs to dying to sins and living for righteousness; the passage does not make mistreatment right.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"1 Peter 2:21-25 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 21,\n      \"text\": \"For you were called to this, because Christ also suffered for you, leaving you an example, that you should follow in his steps.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 22,\n      \"text\": \"He did not commit sin, and no deceit was found in his mouth;\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 23,\n      \"text\": \"when he was insulted, he did not insult in return; when he suffered, he did not threaten but entrusted himself to the one who judges justly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 24,\n      \"text\": \"He himself bore our sins in his body on the tree; so that, having died to sins, we might live for righteousness. By his wounds you have been healed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 25,\n      \"text\": \"For you were like sheep going astray, but you have now returned to the Shepherd and Overseer of your souls.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"1pe\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 2\n}\n```\n\n## Romans 5:1 (CSB)\n\n### Peace with God\n\nTherefore, since we have been justified by faith, we have peace with God through our Lord Jesus Christ.\n\n*Tags: context, faith, love*\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"christmas-csb-45\",\n  \"translation\": \"CSB\",\n  \"locations\": [],\n  \"context_reference\": \"Romans 5:1-11\",\n  \"context_note\": \"Peace with God follows justification by faith. Paul goes on to speak of hope amid affliction and of Christ dying for the ungodly and reconciling enemies to God.\",\n  \"context_selection\": \"Romans 5:1-5 (CSB)\",\n  \"context_verses\": [\n    {\n      \"verse\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"Therefore, since we have been justified by faith, we have peace with God through our Lord Jesus Christ.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 2,\n      \"text\": \"We have also obtained access through him by faith into this grace in which we stand, and we boast in the hope of the glory of God.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 3,\n      \"text\": \"And not only that, but we also boast in our afflictions, because we know that affliction produces endurance,\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 4,\n      \"text\": \"endurance produces proven character, and proven character produces hope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"verse\": 5,\n      \"text\": \"This hope will not disappoint us, because God's love has been poured out in our hearts through the Holy Spirit who was given to us.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_book\": \"rom\",\n  \"source_chapter\": 5\n}\n```\n";
